# ── Sensitive ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit secrets. Solar leaked secrets for 35 days (2026-07-10) because a
# ciphertext store was committed and the key later leaked. Ciphertext + leaked
# key is still a breach. Keep both out of git.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
secrets/
.secrets/

# Per-tenant provider credentials (D7 bring-your-own-connection) are stored
# encrypted in the database, never on disk, never in git.

# ── Node / TypeScript ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.eslintcache

# ── Python (ADK agent host) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# ── Databases / dumps ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sql.gz
*.dump
backups/

# ── Media / uploads (never committed; object storage only) ──────────────────
#
# 🔴 ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING.
#
# These were written unanchored (`media/`), which in gitignore matches a
# directory of that name AT ANY DEPTH. On 2026-08-06 that silently swallowed
# `apps/api/src/media/` — the entire NestJS attachments module: service,
# controller, schemas and module file. `git add -A` reported success, the commit
# listed the migration and both screens, and the four source files it depended
# on were simply absent.
#
# `app.module.ts` imports `./media/media.module`, so the pushed tree could not
# have built. Nothing local noticed: typecheck, lint and the dev server all read
# the working directory, where the files exist. Only `git show HEAD:<path>`
# saying "exists on disk, but not in HEAD" gave it away.
#
# Same family as the ignore rule that once nearly committed two live
# credentials: a pattern written for one thing quietly deciding something else.
# The uploads these lines exist for would live at the repository root, so
# anchoring costs nothing and stops the rule reaching into source trees.
/uploads/
/media/
/quarantine/

# ── Test artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
playwright-report/
test-results/
storybook-static/
*-snapshots/__diff_output__/

# ── Logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
tunnel_*.log

# ── Editor / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.bak_*
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# ── Backup artefacts and the backup encryption key ──────────────────────────
# `.backup-key` does NOT match the `*.key` rule above (it ends in "-key", not
# ".key"). Solar leaked secrets for 35 days in 2026-07; this is the same class
# of mistake, one commit away.
infrastructure/backup/.backup-key
infrastructure/backup/.backup-s3-secret
infrastructure/backup/artifacts/
infrastructure/backup/logs/
infrastructure/backup/status/

# Guardrail runtime state: retrieval index, context packs, raw reviewer output.
# Generated evidence, not source - and the raw transcripts are large.
.guardrails/

# Seam file for the sign-out revocation proof (contains a real dev session)
# Captured sign-in sessions used by the verify/ probes. These are REAL CREDENTIALS —
# an encrypted Auth.js session cookie plus a live Keycloak access token.
#
# ⚠️ A GLOB, NOT ONE FILENAME. `capture-session.mjs --out` (slice 3b) can write any
# name, because proving §1292's reviewer independence needs two sessions alive at
# once — and `.verify-tech-cookies.json` / `.verify-sup-cookies.json` were staged by
# `git add -A` on the very first run, since the old exact-match line did not cover
# them. One filename in an ignore file is a rule that holds only until somebody adds
# a second file.
.verify-*cookies*.json
.verify-session-cookies.json

# Backup-drill runtime lock — holds a live PID and timestamp, so it is machine
# state, never source. Swept into a commit once by a `git add -A`.
infrastructure/backup/.lock-*/

# Expo's per-machine dev-server state (`devices.json` records the devices that
# have opened this project). Generated by `expo start`, never source. A GLOB on
# the directory, not the two filenames it happens to hold today — the lesson
# recorded above the `.verify-*cookies*` line applies identically here.
apps/mobile/.expo/

# 🔴 REAL ENVIRONMENT FILES. `.env` holds POSTGRES_PASSWORD, DATABASE_URL and
# AUTH_SECRET. Until now NOTHING in this file protected it — it stayed out of
# the repo by discipline alone, and a single `git add -A` would have committed
# live credentials. This repo has already had that near-miss once (see the
# `.verify-*cookies*` note above), so the rule is a PATTERN, not a filename:
# any future `.env.local`, `.env.production` etc. is covered the day it is made.
# `.env.example` is the documented template and carries placeholders only, so it
# is explicitly re-included.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated at image-build time by build-prod-realm.mjs. It is a DERIVED file —
# committing it would create a second realm to keep in step with the real one,
# and the stale copy is the one that would get deployed.
infrastructure/keycloak/render/realm-prod.json

# Local Mailpit STARTTLS material — generated by scripts/dev-mailpit-cert.sh.
# Never committed: a private key in a public repo is an incident this project
# has already had once.
infrastructure/docker/mailpit-tls/
